4","HVNp3ms","he was terrified"],["מִפְּנֵי","mipenei","H6440","HR/Ncmpc","of <the face of>"],["חֶרֶב","cherev","H2719","HNcfsc","[the] sword of"],["מַלְאַךְ","mal'akh","H4397","HNcmsc","[the] angel of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"]],"x":[[58012028,58012029,3],[66001017,66001017,3],[66015004,66015004,3]],"xn":3}},"people":[{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[1,2,5,8,9,10,11,13,16,17,18,19,21,22,23,24,25,26,28,30]},{"id":"satan_2476","name":"Satan","also":"Beelzebub","summary":"Adversary; accuser. When used as a proper name, the Hebrew word so rendered has the article “the adversary” (Job 1:6-12; 2:1-7).","verses":55,"father":"","mother":"","v":[1]},{"id":"joab_1617","name":"Joab","also":"","summary":"One of the three sons of Zeruiah, David’s sister, and “captain of the host” during the whole of David’s reign (2 Sam. 2:13; 10:7; 11:1; 1 Kings 11:15).","verses":119,"father":"","mother":"Zeruiah","v":[2,3,4,5,6]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[2]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[6]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[6]},{"id":"gad_1263","name":"Gad","also":"","summary":"A prophet who joined David in the “hold,” and at whose advice he quitted it for the forest of Hareth (1 Chr. 29:29; 2 Chr. 29:25; 1 Sam. 22:5).","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9,11,13,18,19]},{"id":"ornan_289","name":"Ornan","also":"Araunah","summary":"Agile; also called Ornan 1 Chr. 21:15, a Jebusite who dwelt in Jerusalem before it was taken by the Israelites. The destroying angel, sent to punish David for his vanity in taking a census of the people, was stayed in his work of destruction near a threshing-floor belonging to Araunah which was situated on Mount Moriah.","verses":17,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15,18,20,21,22,23,24,25,28]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[29]}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[2]},{"id":"dan_323","name":"Dan","kind":"Region","lat":33.24856,"lon":35.65252,"summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":20,"v":[2]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[4,15,16]},{"id":"gibeon_470","name":"Gibeon","kind":"City","lat":31.84668,"lon":35.1852,"summary":"Hill-city, “one of the royal cities, greater than Ai, and all the men thereof were mighty” (Josh. 10:2). Its inhabitants were Hivites (11:19).","verses":35,"v":[29]}],"even